{
  "$comment": "Cross-language SSoT for webhook signature V2 (X-Faas-Signature-V2). `cases` are the server's signing vectors, computed independently (Python hmac/hashlib): every header a delivery carries for a given secret, unix timestamp and raw body. Bodies are opaque UTF-8 bytes; verify over them exactly. `verification` is what a receiver must decide for (secret, raw body, header, now): accept when some v1 equals HMAC-SHA256(secret, \"<t>.<body>\") and |now - t| <= tolerance_sec. Every SDK must reproduce both sections.",
  "contract_version": "2.3.0",
  "algorithm": "HMAC-SHA256",
  "encoding": "lowercase-hex",
  "header": "X-Faas-Signature-V2",
  "format": "t=<unix seconds>,v1=<hex hmac_sha256(secret, \"<t>.<raw body>\")>[,v1=<same, previous secret during a rotation>]",
  "tolerance_sec": 300,
